[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270100607","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118691#issuecomment-4270100607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118691","id":4270100607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-hJB_","user":{"login":"Rafael-Duarte-Silva","id":38193394,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MTkzMzk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38193394?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva","html_url":"https://github.com/Rafael-Duarte-Silva","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rafael-Duarte-Silva/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T17:43:11Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T17:43:11Z","body":"While investigating, I found that handling FocusOut in platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp (inside process_events) can mitigate the issue with a simple approach like:\n\n``` c++\nfor (auto &E : windows) {\n    if (E.value.is_popup) {\n        XUnmapWindow(x11_display, E.value.x11_window);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis effectively hides all popup windows when focus is lost, which resolves the immediate problem.\n\nHowever, I’m not fully familiar with the popup lifecycle in Godot, and I’m not sure if this approach is correct or complete. In particular:\n\nIt may bypass expected popup management (e.g., proper close notifications, state updates, or signals).\nIt might not respect how popups are supposed to be dismissed internally (e.g., via Popup::hide() or higher-level UI logic).\nThere could be edge cases with nested popups or transient relationships.\n\nSo while this workaround appears to fix the visual issue, I’m unsure if it aligns with the intended design of popup handling in the engine.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4270100607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4273087312","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118691#issuecomment-4273087312","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118691","id":4273087312,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-siNQ","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":fal